Package: rsimd
Title: SIMD-Accelerated Vector Primitives
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Simon", "Potter", email = "simon@sjp.co.nz", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Evan", "Nemerson", role = "cph", comment = "SIMDe"),
    person("SIMDe authors", role = "cph", comment = "SIMDe, see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
  )
Description: Fast vectorised primitives for R atomic vectors, including
    reductions, elementwise arithmetic, predicates, bitwise operations,
    conversions and transcendental functions, implemented with single
    instruction, multiple data (SIMD) instructions on x86-64 and arm64.
    Kernels are written once using the portable 'SIMDe' intrinsics library
    and use 'SLEEF' for vectorised elementary functions. CPU features are
    detected at run time and the best supported implementation is chosen
    automatically, while users can select a specific implementation, or a
    plain scalar one, by name.
